      {"kind": "image", "slot": "hero", "rect": [48, 202, 517, 250]},
      {"kind": "text", "slot": "kicker", "rect": [48, 471.54, 517, 13], "style": "Kicker", "sample": "Around the commons"},
      {"kind": "text", "slot": "title", "rect": [48, 478.57, 517, 100], "style": "Lead Title", "sample": "The orchard is back, and it needs pickers"},
      {"kind": "text", "slot": "subtitle", "rect": [48, 575.1, 517, 39], "style": "Lead Deck", "sample": "Six years after the storm, the old trees by the mill pond are heavy with fruit again. Here is how to help bring it in."},
      {"kind": "text", "flow": "body", "rect": [48, 627, 517, 242], "style": "Bul Body", "columns": 3, "gutter": 20, "sample": ["When the great storm of 2020 took down half the trees in the community orchard, plenty of people thought it was the end of it. A small group of volunteers thought otherwise. They cleared the fallen trunks, grafted cuttings from the survivors and planted forty young trees in the gaps.", "This autumn, for the first time, the new trees are cropping properly. There are russets, cooking apples, two kinds of pear and a quince that nobody remembers planting. There is far more fruit than the orchard group can pick on its own.", "Picking mornings run every Saturday in October from 10 am, starting at the gate by the mill pond. Ladders, gloves and tea are provided; bring a bag and you can take a share home. Children are welcome with an adult, and the last Saturday ends with a pressing and a bonfire.", "Any fruit that is not taken home goes to the food bank on Station Road and to the school kitchen, which has promised a crumble for every class."]},
